text I open my eyes and see that I'm in my room.
text I feel like I was having a bad dream.
text I'm drenched in sweat.
text With my head still on my pillow, I look around.
text The light only faintly illuminates the room, making it hard to tell if it's sunrise or sunset.
text I lean over and look at the clock to see what time it is.
text May 8th, Thursday morning...
text I feel tired.
text I vaguely remember brooding and worrying until late into the night.
text Suddenly, it all comes back to me.
text It's only been one day since the incident.
text I can't believe it.
text Kotomi just crumpled to the ground and started sobbing.
text Then she went home on her own without saying anything to me.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I flop back onto the bed again.
text Feelings of confusion keep washing over me.
text It's like back when I couldn't help but run away despite having nowhere to go.
text I knew that there wasn't a solution, but I thought something would change if I only kept worrying about it.
text I was the only one who thought that was acceptable.
text If I fall back asleep now...
text I won't feel like going to school when I wake up.
text That's how I lie to myself to take my mind off my problems.
text I get out of bed.
text I sluggishly put on my uniform.
text I don't want to escape into that fog of uncertainty anymore.
