text I stop at the intersection where I normally part ways with Kotomi.
text Trying to catch my breath, I take the piece of paper out of my pocket.
text The note indicates a place I'm not familiar with.
text I spent all of the afternoon classes looking at this piece of paper instead of listening to the teachers.
text I doubt that Kotomi has to walk too far from where we part ways.
text I'm confident I can find it. No, I HAVE to find it.
text I continue on with the paper clutched in my hand.
