text The garden is in disarray.
text The grass has been left uncut and weeds of all kinds have grown tall.
text A couple of garden chairs sit next to a tilting table.
text The paint has crusted off, showing dark red rust.
text The wind, brought by the dusk, blows through the forgotten ruins of this place.
text I can't do anything but stand here.
text This isn't how it's supposed to be.
text The grass was always cleanly cut.
text The chairs and table were painted bright white.
text A brick wall surrounded a flower bed full of blooming flowers.
text A dreamland had always awaited me.
text There's an opening at the corner of the hedge that I used to use as my way in.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...?!
text What is this?
text This feeling... I think they call it deja vu.
text I know this place.
text But I don't know how I know it.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I push through the weeds and silently take one step at a time.
text The overgrown grass tangles my feet, trying to block my path.
text I need to go to the living room facing the garden.
text A tall glass door with a wooden frame separates the inside from the outside world.
text The curtain is closed, blocking me from seeing what's inside.
text As if it's some sort of signal, I notice that the far edge of the glass door is open just a crack.
text That's probably the same as it was in the past.
text I pull at the sliding door with all of my strength and it creaks loudly.
text It moves to the side, little by little.
text I take off my shoes and enter the living room.
