text It's dark inside.
text The wooden flooring is engulfed by the stale, dusty air.
text It has the mysterious smell of faded western sunrays.
text I focus my eyes and look around.
text There's a table in the middle of the room surrounded by a sofa, and a side table rests against the wall.
text Their textures are completely gone, as if they're carved from stone.
text I'm sure they haven't been touched in years.
text I cautiously press on deeper past the living room.
text In the middle of the hallway is a set of stairs.
text Each step takes me slowly upward.
text I still have this bizarre feeling of being drawn forward by memories that don't belong to me.
text I tiptoe toward a door at the far end of the second floor.
text I still don't understand how I know this place.
text And...
text I stand in front of the farthest door.
text I fumble at the doorknob and turn it. It isn't locked.
text This is also the same as it's always been.
text I slowly open the door.
