text This was when I was still small.
text Around sunset, when the wind starts to get cold, my mother and father were talking in the garden.
text I loved the prickly feeling of walking barefoot through the grass.
text I loved the warm light and the smell of the earth and grass.
text I loved the white shiny chairs and table.
sound DXB.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Why is my name Kotomi?
text With the pipe in his mouth, my father thought deeply.
text I loved seeing my father when he was like that.
text No matter how insignificant the question, my father always answered me.
sound DXC.aac
text @[Father]
text Take a look, Kotomi.
text My father pointed at the sky.
text I squinted a little and looked up with him.
text The sky was vast and so, so high.
text There were orange clouds and a gentle wind.
sound DXD.aac
text @[Father]
text The world is formed by many very tiny harps that are invisible to the naked eye.
sound DXE.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Lots of... harps?
sound DXF.aac
text @[Father]
text Yes. In the language of this country, the word we use is "koto."
sound DXG.aac
text @[Father]
text The world is filled with harps, and each and every one plays a different kind of sound.
sound DXH.aac
text @[Father]
text And they all intertwine in a complex way to form a single melody.
sound DXI.aac
text @[Father]
text That is why this world is so beautiful.
sound DXJ.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Who is playing the harps?
sound DXK.aac
text @[Father]
text That's a very difficult question...
text My father went back to thinking deeply.
text He held up his pipe and puffed out smoke.
text The branches of the garden's trees waved in the wind, dappling the grass with shadows.
text The shadows also shimmered on my father's gray hair, my mother's pale fingers, and my legs.
sound DXL.aac
text @[Father]
text Probably God, I think.
text That was my father's answer.
sound DXM.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Where is God?
sound DXN.aac
text @[Father]
text God is everywhere. We just can't see him.
sound DXO.aac
text @[Father]
text And he's always kindly watching over us.
sound DXP.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Um...
text I thought long and hard about what my father said.
text Lots of harps that are invisible to the eye.
text A kind God that is invisible to the eye.
sound DXQ.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text That's very, very confusing.
sound DXR.aac
text @[Father]
text It's okay to think that for now.
sound DXS.aac
text @[Father]
text There are many other things you need to learn first, Kotomi.
text His large, rugged hands patted me on the head.
text On the chair next to my father, my mother was smiling.
sound DXT.aac
text @[Mother]
text You have a bad habit of explaining things in such grandiose ways.
sound DXU.aac
text @[Mother]
text The most important things are always the simplest.
sound DXV.aac
text @[Mother]
text Right, dear?
text My mother winked, which made my father smile bashfully.
text My mother then picked me up and put me on her lap.
text Her snow-white apron smelled faintly of soap.
sound DXW.aac
text @[Mother]
text Kotomi-chan, Kotomi-chan.
sound DXX.aac
text @[Mother]
text A very beautiful three hiragana letters.
sound DXY.aac
text @[Mother]
text Mommy and Daddy's precious, precious treasure...
text I loved my mother's voice because it always reverberated like a song to me.
text My mother's cheek was ticklish, soft, and warm...
text I was so happy.
