text My mother and father, at our home in the garden with freshly cut grass.
text That was my whole world.
text Even when I entered elementary school, that didn't change.
text When I tried reading the books on the teacher's desk, the boys made fun of me.
sound VYI.aac
text Those books are for grown-ups, so kids aren't allowed to read them.
text @And even the teachers who ran to me said...
sound VYJ.aac
text Let's read the same books as everyone else.
text I cried.
text I didn't know there were books I shouldn't read. I had already finished reading all the books in the classroom on the first day.
text Wanting to stay home from school, I said my stomach hurt.
text My mother and father didn't force me to go.
text I got over my sickness right away, but my heart hurt in its place.
text It's because I was lying.
delay 60
text Even though we didn't go to the same school, I made a friend.
text I was rehearsing my violin by myself in the living room.
text My recital was coming up, so I was wearing the dress my mother had sewn for me.
text The black, silky cloth made me feel like a big girl, so it was one of my favorites.
text After finishing my performance, a boy I had never seen before was in the yard looking at me.
setvar strS[1000] = "BG051K"
