text Whenever evening approached, Tomoya-kun would visit me.
text He would always come into the garden through the gap in the hedge like a stray cat.
text I looked forward to Tomoya-kun visiting every day.
text I loved reading together and playing house.
text I loved playing hide-and-seek and tag in the yard.
text Tomoya-kun didn't seem to like any of those games, though.
text But he would always try his best to play with me.
text Whenever we were indoors, my mother would always make sweets for us.
text I ate cakes, cookies, and cream puffs with Tomoya-kun.
text I always did halfsies with Tomoya-kun.
text Whenever it got dark, Tomoya-kun would go back home.
text And whenever I said "see you tomorrow," he would look troubled.
text And he would always say, "I might not come tomorrow."
text I loved Tomoya-kun.
text There were times when he didn't visit, but he would come most of the time.
