text May 13th was my birthday.
text My father promised to buy me a large teddy bear.
text I read in a book that girls typically wanted things like that.
text In truth, I didn't care what the present was.
text I loved the wonderful books that my father bought for me the best.
text I might have already realized this back then...
text I was somewhat different from Tomoya-kun and the others at school.
text Maybe that's why I wanted to be with them.
text I wanted to make many more friends.
text When I told that to Tomoya-kun, he promised me that he would definitely come to my party.
text I looked forward to it very, very much.
text But...
text Tomoya-kun never came and I never got my teddy bear.
text My mother and father had sudden business to attend to, and they were going overseas.
delay 60
sound DYM.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Daddy, you're a liar!
sound DYN.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Mommy... I hate you!
sound DYO.aac
text @[Mother]
text I'm sorry, Kotomi.
sound DYP.aac
text @[Mother]
text This is something that we have to do.
sound DYQ.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But...
sound DYR.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But you promised.
sound DYS.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text You promised that you'd be with me on my birthday.
sound DYT.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text You said you'd give me a big teddy bear...
sound DYU.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text And we'd have a birthday party.
sound DYV.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text And you said I could call Tomoya-kun...
text No matter what arguments I made, my mother and father wouldn't cancel their trip.
sound DYW.aac
text @[Mother]
text There's a feast for you in the refrigerator.
sound DYX.aac
text @[Mother]
text I made lots of food that's good even when it's cold.
sound DYY.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you.
sound DYZ.aac
text @[Mother]
text Eat it with Tomoya-kun when he comes to visit.
sound DZ0.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you.
sound DZ1.aac
text @[Mother]
text The maid will be coming, too. If you need anything, be sure to tell her.
sound DZ2.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you...
text I watched as my mother and father put on their shoes.
text A suitcase was placed in the hallway.
text It was my father's usual suitcase.
text It was a shiny silver suitcase he used to put important things in.
sound DZ3.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you.
sound DZ4.aac
text @[Mother]
text Kotomi-chan...
text My mother looked so sad.
text My father said nothing.
sound DZ5.aac
text @[Mother]
text I know. Before we get on the airplane, we'll look for a teddy bear for you.
sound DZ6.aac
text @[Mother]
text If we ship it from the airport, you'll get it on your birthday.
sound DZ7.aac
text @[Mother]
text I'll send you the biggest teddy bear we can find.
sound DZ8.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I don't want it.
sound DZ9.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I don't want anything!
text What I really wanted wasn't a teddy bear.
text I wanted my mother and father to be with me.
text I wanted them to be with me and Tomoya-kun to celebrate my birthday.
sound DZA.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you, Mommy and Daddy.
sound DZB.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you...
sound DZC.aac
text @[Mother]
text We won't be gone long. We'll be home really soon.
sound DZD.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I hate you... I hate you...
text All I did was repeat "I hate you."
text It's as if I had forgotten any other words.
text I thought that saying that would maybe keep them with me.
sound DZE.aac
text @[Father]
text Kotomi...
sound DZF.aac
text @[Father]
text Be a good girl and wait for us.
text My father gently placed his hand on my head.
