text I gathered my courage and turned on the television.
text The television wouldn't ring on its own and I could turn it off whenever I wanted.
text There were pictures of my mother and father on the screen.
sound VYK.aac
text "Since the days when they were professor and assistant at the laboratory, the Ichinoses had recognized each other's talents. They soon married and..."
text There were pictures of my mother and father from when they were much younger than I'd ever seen before.
sound VYL.aac
text "The accident occurred soon after hastily scheduling a special lecture at the academic society."
text Then there was a long list of names.
text The television said that the airplane had fallen into the ocean where it was very deep and cold. The chances of survival were very slim if they had been thrown into the water.
sound VYM.aac
text "With regards to the missing persons, considering the circumstances of the crash, it is unlikely that there are any survivors."
text I turned off the television.
text A crackling noise came from the television.
text My father told me before that it was static electricity and that it was nothing to be afraid of.
text But for some reason, I was a little scared of it right now.
text Now that the television was off, it wasn't making any more noises.
text I felt as if I was being sucked in.
text Being alone scared me.
text I was much more afraid of that than I was of the adults or the sound of the telephone.
