delay 60
text When night came, my stomach growled.
text I decided to eat dinner.
text I opened the refrigerator and lined the plates of food on the table.
text Tomoya-kun might not come today.
text But he will surely come tomorrow.
text I carefully halved the spaghetti salad, roast pork, and stewed sweet potatoes.
text I was saving it for Tomoya-kun.
sound E17.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Let us eat.
sound E18.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Let's eat.
text After putting my palms together, I had a realization.
text What would I do when all of the meals were gone?
text Mommy would come back and make more for me...
sound E19.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Oh...
text I finally understood.
text My mother and father weren't coming back.
text This is the last I would ever eat of my mother's cooking.
text Tears fell from my cheeks.
text They streamed down my face and wouldn't stop.
text So I ate while I cried.
text Eating while crying made everything taste salty and not good.
text That made more tears fall from my cheeks.
